# HP-16C: CHS stack-lift fix. Credit: Thomas Klemm found the bug and wrote the first patches
# (HP-15C 2015-12-12, HP-11C and HP-16C 2015-12-14; MoHPC forum, thread 5321 "HP-15C: Fixing the
# CHS and Stack Lift Bug"). Amphitryon checked the 11C patch against a firmware trace and
# corrected its jumps (same thread), passed this 16C version on to us and says he completed it;
# which word is whose we cannot tell.
# Bug: when X is 0, CHS does not clear the "stack lift disabled" flag,
# so after CLx (or BSP) "CHS 7" overwrites X instead of lifting the stack.
# Shows in FLOAT mode: f FLOAT .  3 ENTER 4 g CLx CHS 7 +
#   original 16C: 1.000000 01 (10)   patched: 7.000000 00 (7)
# For: original HP-16C ROM (Nonpareil ncd/16c/16c.rom),
#   fingerprint bbccd62ebc2da37688cbaa631b6fe38664896467a4aff676552ec51e17e7631d
# 9 code words in 0C8C-0CE9, plus 006F so the chip checksum stays right.
006f:390
0c8c:183
0c96:137
0caf:05b
0cb8:01b
0cb9:2be
0cba:0f0
0cbc:251
0cbd:002
0ce9:28b
